+
+## Deploying on one server
+
+Fizzy includes a [Kamal](https://kamal-deploy.org/) configuration for running the
+web app, background jobs, SQLite databases, and file storage on one Linux server.
+The server needs Docker, SSH access, and DNS pointed at it; Kamal Proxy handles
+HTTPS certificates and renewal.
+
+1. In `config/deploy.yml`, replace `YOUR_SERVER_IP`, both occurrences of
+   `YOUR_DOCKER_HUB_USERNAME`, `fizzy.example.com` (in both `proxy.host` and
+   `APP_HOST`), the sender address, and the SMTP server settings.
+2. Export the four values referenced by `.kamal/secrets`:
+
+   ```sh
+   export KAMAL_REGISTRY_PASSWORD='...'
+   export SECRET_KEY_BASE="$(bin/rails secret)"
+   export SMTP_USERNAME='...'
+   export SMTP_PASSWORD='...'
+   ```
+
+3. Push the initial image and provision the server:
+
+   ```sh
+   bin/kamal setup
+   ```
+
+Fizzy will be available at `https://fizzy.example.com` (using your replacement
+hostname). The named `fizzy_storage` Docker volume contains every SQLite database
+and uploaded file, so it is retained across deploys. Back up this volume regularly.
+Solid Queue runs inside Puma for this one-container setup; no Redis or separate
+jobs server is required.
